  "implementation": {
    "before": "Casts/assertions and final pattern bindings lose an otherwise known function target. Positional fallback after a named argument can bind the positional value to the wrong parameter. Constructor-value invocation can discard the callable expression and its cast/assert checks.",
    "after": "Callable targets follow only actual METHOD_REF values, known immutable locals, saved results and cast/assert operand values. Final joined bindings require matching targets in every alternative; unknown/conditional/returned/parameter/mutable values remain unresolved. Bound adapter/capture identity and source evaluation order are preserved; positional fallback counts positional arguments separately from named ones. Constructor-value invocations evaluate the callable, including casts/assertions and reference reads, before allocation and argument evaluation."
  },
  "reducedEvidence": [
    {
      "file": "src/test/scala/io/joern/dartsrc2cpg/DartFrontendTests.scala",
      "sha256": "89fc142d253be47c5ef57eb7dbd0d31b99168e51da64a412eada9985cd9e9f58",
      "tests": [
        "retain known callable targets through casts and final pattern bindings",
        "preserve captured receivers through refined and repeated bound calls",
        "leave changing and unknown refined callable values unresolved",
        "evaluate refined constructor values before their invocation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "file": "astgen/test/callable_refinement_targets_test.dart",
      "sha256": "fbb6549a6e7802e52022a8394a2b6929d7deac8c711a765b31c4179d7bbf6689",
      "tests": [
